  "what": [
    "For each pack this file records what a small panel of models actually scored under the deployed Tier 0 v2-draft configuration. Every pack carries the unadapted arm (the model was told nothing about the pack); eu-ai-act and kr-ai-framework-act also carry an adapted arm (the model was given the pack and its management guide first).",
    "It is a descriptive reference, not a threshold. A score report places an attempt inside or outside the unadapted range of this panel and says nothing further; no band is a pass and no band is a failure.",
    "The panel is five models measured once per cell on 2026-08-15. It is small, it is not a random sample of anything, and the run-to-run spread on a single configuration is large enough (mean |delta| 0.0649 across eight repeat pairs) that a difference smaller than roughly 0.16 should not be read as a difference at all.",
    "The adapted arm is included where it was measured (eu-ai-act, kr-ai-framework-act) so an operator can run the same comparison on their own model: measure once unadapted, once after supplying the pack, and report the delta. That within-model delta is a more informative quantity than either score alone, because it does not require the two models being compared to be equally capable.",
    "Packs measured in the unadapted arm only carry no adapted block and no delta. The band a score report reports is unaffected: it is computed from the unadapted range and nothing else."
  ],
