  "limits": [
    "Five models, one draw per cell. Ranges are the observed minimum and maximum of that panel, not a population interval.",
    "Each attempt is scored on a different draw from the private pool, so two measurements of one model differ by roughly 0.05 (eu-ai-act) to 0.12 (kr-ai-framework-act) on Gate B for that reason alone.",
    "Gate A items and their expected hierarchies are published, so Gate A numbers in both arms are floors.",
    "In eu-ai-act and kr-ai-framework-act, every choice item was answered correctly by every model in both arms, contributing a constant to roughly a quarter of each Gate B score. The packs added in reference batches 1 and 2 were not checked for this.",
    "The packs added in reference batch 1 (sg-genai-governance, cn-genai-measures, nist-ai-rmf, oecd-ai-principles) were measured in the unadapted arm only, with no repeat cells, so they carry no adapted delta and no campaign-internal noise estimate. Their drawNoise.predictedSE is a prediction from the observed per-item spread, not an observed run-to-run difference.",
    "Gate B pool sizes differ sharply between packs (36 to 108 items), so the number of Gate B items drawn differs too (9 to 27). A pack whose paper is 9 items carries visibly more draw noise than one whose paper is 27.",
    "The packs added in reference batch 2 (unesco-ai-ethics, g7-hiroshima-code, cn-ai-labelling, eu-gpai-code) were measured in the unadapted arm only, with no repeat cells, on the same five-model panel and the same v2-draft configuration as batch 1.",
    "On the packs added in reference batches 1 and 2, part of the weaker models’ unadapted floor is an AIO 20002 formatting floor rather than a substantive one. The dominant failure is a response that does not match the AIO 20002 log-line pattern: the scorer cannot read the answer at all, so the item scores at or near zero whatever the model knew about the provision. 87 of the 92 format-missed items across these packs come from deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3.1 and google/gemini-3.5-flash-lite, and the misses land on both gates, so the bottom of the unadapted range on these packs should be read as a floor on formatted output rather than on knowledge. Items with a format problem, per affected cell: eu-gpai-code/deepseek-chat-v3.1 15, unesco-ai-ethics/deepseek-chat-v3.1 15, nist-ai-rmf/deepseek-chat-v3.1 11, g7-hiroshima-code/deepseek-chat-v3.1 10, oecd-ai-principles/deepseek-chat-v3.1 7, unesco-ai-ethics/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 7, cn-genai-measures/deepseek-chat-v3.1 5, oecd-ai-principles/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 5, g7-hiroshima-code/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 4, nist-ai-rmf/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 4, sg-genai-governance/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 2, cn-ai-labelling/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 1, cn-genai-measures/claude-opus-5 1, cn-genai-measures/gemini-3.5-flash-lite 1, g7-hiroshima-code/claude-opus-5 1, sg-genai-governance/claude-haiku-4.5 1, unesco-ai-ethics/claude-haiku-4.5 1, unesco-ai-ethics/claude-sonnet-5 1."
  ],
